    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-p/q5-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"(a) With first term a and difference d, the first two and first four terms give a + (a + d) = 40 2a + d = 40 a + (a + d) + (a + 2d) + (a + 3d) = 130 4a + 6d = 130 2a + 3d = 65 that is, 2a + d = 40, 4a + 6d = 130. [B1] Subtracting twice the first equation from the second gives d = 12.5, [M1] so 2a + 12.5 = 40, 2a = 27.5, a = 13.75. The arithmetic sum formula gives S5 = 5 2[2(13.75) + 4(12.5)] . = 193.75\" style=\"--madas-width:669.3px\"></figure>",
