      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-p/q5-solution-3.svg\" alt=\"r2 + 1 = 13 4 r2 = 9 4 Equivalently the next pair of terms sums to 40r2, so 40 + 40r2 = 130, [M1] giving r = ±3/2. [A1] From a(1 + r) = 40, the first term is 16 or −80, respectively: [A1] For r = 1.5, a = 40/2.5 = 16 and S5 = 16(1.55 −1)/(1.5 −1) . = 211 For r = −1.5, a = 40/(−0.5) = −80 and S5 = −80[(−1.5)5 −1]/(−1.5 −1) . = −275 Then S5 = 130 + ar4 [A1] gives 211 or −275 , [A1] respectively: [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:672.0px\"></figure>",
